  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Landscape conservation of western chimpanzees in the Moyen-Bafing National Park, Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this 1-year project is to protect the largest population of critically endangered western chimpanzees by completing the process of establishing the proposed Moyen-Bafing National Park. Activities include: 1) strengthening the involvement, and building the capacity, of surrounding communities in protection of the park and its natural resources; 2) creating local committees to facilitate regional and local stakeholder consultations; 3) implementing eco-friendly agricultural practices; 4) conducting participatory mapping missions to identify the community boundaries and to cultivate community support; 5) monitoring chimpanzee populations; 6) determining baseline land cover data; 7) implementing habitat regeneration and reforestation measures to maintain headwaters integrity; and 8) studying the effects of seasonal fires on the parks habitat.</narrative>
  </description>
